WEBVTT

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.080
My name is Ryoma Takebayashi.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.620
I'm 11.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:38.000
I live alone in the forest.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.330
No, I'm not alone...

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:47.370
I live with almost a thousand slimes!

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:55.250
Slimes evolve differently
depending on what you feed them.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:01:00.120
I fed green caterpillars to some of them
and they turned into sticky slimes.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.500
The sticky fluid they form inside their bodies

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:09.830
can be used to make a powerful thread
that's helpful for hunting.

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:17.080
Acid slimes have highly acidic body fluids
that can dissolve hard things like bones.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:24.040
Poison slimes are the result of slimes
that ate poisonous weeds and survived.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:29.000
They must have a strong vitality,
because they split faster than other slimes.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.620
Cleaner slimes clean things
by eating dirt and grime.

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:34.620
They even get rid of smells.

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:41.290
Scavenger slimes eat excrement
and garbage to make fertilizer.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:04.830
Well... sometimes I run into goblins
and thieves and have to fight them...

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:11.120
...but every day is the same: nice and peaceful.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:13.250
Don't die on us, Hughes!

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:14.620
--Hughes!
--Hughes!

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:16.000
--This life is going to continue forever...

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.160
--Don't die, Hughes!
--This life is going to continue forever...

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:22.950
That's what I thought.

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:58.000
"Episode 1"
"Ryoma, with the Slimes"

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:04.200
Bandits? No...

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.950
What are they doing this deep in the forest?

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.080
Well, Camil?

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:17.500
I'm sorry. I don't have enough
magic left to heal him...

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:20.040
We need to hurry and get him back to town.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:22.080
He won't last long.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:23.540
Um...

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.120
Who are you?

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.120
Um...

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:33.910
What's a kid doing out here?

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:37.790
I haven't talked to anyone
in so many years that my voice...

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:42.040
Um... Medicine. Me have.

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:44.290
Why am I talking like a caveman?

00:04:44.290 --> 00:04:45.700
Medicine?

00:04:46.790 --> 00:04:49.620
This. Medicine.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:51.160
Hurry.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:06.830
Well?

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:07.910
It's fine.

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:09.790
This is medicine, I'm sure of it.

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:18.290
Hughes?

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:19.790
He's just asleep.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:22.120
He'll be fine for a while.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.700
Thank you.

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:26.750
Home. Can rest.

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:28.120
Will rest.

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:30.700
You're sure?

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:36.250
What's he doing in this forest?

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:38.790
He's dressed like a hunter.

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:40.790
Does he live alone?

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:43.000
What's wrong?

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.830
Looks like beast came this way.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:46.160
Will come soon.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:47.580
Who will?

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:53.080
A horde of slimes!

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:56.910
Enemy! Not!

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:02.910
Are those slimes your servants?

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:09.580
Sorry.

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:12.370
I didn't know they were your familiars.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:18.950
I remember having slimes.

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:22.410
They were my first familiars.

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:24.410
A tamer?

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:26.540
Former tamer.

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:30.000
My family have been tamers for generations.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:35.370
We used to have red horses
and blizzard apes for familiars.

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.200
A noble.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:40.830
Is he important, maybe?

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:46.250
This looks like a dead end.

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:47.950
Where's your house?

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:49.950
Wait. Please.

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:58.830
Come in.

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:02.000
Barrier magic, to hide his home?

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.200
Yup.

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:07.910
This house is pretty impressive.

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:09.120
Yes.

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:12.120
He should be able to rest here.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:14.160
Something's weird here.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:15.790
Zeph, what's wrong?

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:18.910
There's only enough furniture for one.

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:20.620
True.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:23.000
Does he live here alone?

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:24.160
Impossible.

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:28.200
The way he was able to get close
without us noticing him,

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:29.580
his magic...

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:33.000
He may not be as young as he appears.

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:38.290
Use this.

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:39.540
Thanks.

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:41.580
We'll repay you for this another time.

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:43.370
No. Can make these.

00:07:43.370 --> 00:07:44.580
Take all you like.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:46.330
Make them?

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:48.950
You made these potions?

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:50.790
Yes.

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:52.200
What are you?

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.580
Um... Oh, I know!

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:57.370
Do you want some water?

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:58.580
Ice?

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:01.120
You can use ice magic?

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:02.830
Who are you?

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:05.250
I couldn't change the subject!

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:08.750
Um... my name. Ryoma.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:11.120
I apologize.

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:13.950
My name is Reinhart Jamil.

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:16.410
The ruler of the Jamil Duchy.

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:17.790
A duke?

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:19.540
I-I'm sorry!

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:22.370
No, no need to bow.

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:25.120
I'm in your debt.

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:26.370
Okay...

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:28.450
I thought he was important.

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:30.580
But I didn't realize he was a duke!

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:32.910
I'm Camil, a mage.

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:34.080
Nice to meet you.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:37.450
And thanks for helping Hughes.

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:39.700
I'm Zeph, a scout.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:41.910
Nice to meet you, kid.

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:43.000
I'm Jill.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:45.500
I apologize for drawing my sword on you.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:49.370
No. Caution... is natural.

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:51.500
It's kind of you to say that.

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:53.830
No... By the way...

00:08:53.830 --> 00:08:56.500
We were struck by bandits outside the forest.

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:57.910
And that's how he got hurt?

00:08:57.910 --> 00:09:01.040
No, the bandits were nothing.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:03.370
But a black bear came out of the forest.

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:05.000
And that's how...

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:09.790
We beat the black bear, but our horses fled.

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:11.700
We wanted to get Hughes to town
as fast as possible,

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:13.540
so we decided to cut through the forest.

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:16.040
And that's how we met you.

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:18.950
Can we ask a question, too?

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:20.620
Okay...

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:22.580
What are you doing here?

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:26.750
You can use multiple types of magic,
and even make potions.

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:28.870
Um...

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:32.410
I learned from my grandparents.

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:34.700
Former adventurers.

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:36.450
I see.

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:38.910
And they're both out at the moment?

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:41.160
They died.

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:42.410
Three years ago.

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:43.620
Three years?

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:46.410
Before they died, they said,

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:48.750
"Go to another village."

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:53.620
I'm an outsider. The villagers don't like me.

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:56.080
I understand.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:57.410
But...

00:09:57.410 --> 00:10:00.620
I don't see how you can
survive alone in the forest.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:01.580
I'm fine.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:03.700
I've survived three years.

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:04.830
But...

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:07.580
I know! I've got just the thing.

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:11.750
This crystal shines red if
the person that touches it is a criminal.

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:15.040
It shines blue if they're not.

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:18.540
It also tells you their name, race, and age,

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:22.250
and four of their high-level skills.

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:28.160
If you have powerful combat skills,
no one will oppose you living in the forest.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:30.080
Okay.

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:35.540
Okay, you're no criminal.

00:10:35.540 --> 00:10:37.540
Wh-What is this?

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:38.790
What's wrong?

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:41.000
Um...

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:44.450
I'm afraid you don't have any combat skills.

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:46.450
I see.

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:49.330
I'll get dinner ready.

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:51.500
Thanks.

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:53.330
Look at this.

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:55.120
Age 11?

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:59.080
Which means he's been alone since he was eight?

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:02.620
That's surprising on its own,
but look at the skills.

00:11:02.620 --> 00:11:04.830
Housekeeping, level 10.

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:07.870
Mental pain resistance, 9.

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:10.790
Physical pain resistance, 8!

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:14.950
What kind of life has he lived at his age?

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:18.080
We can't leave him here.

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:21.410
But what do we do?

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:26.330
I'll head home and then
talk to Father and Elise.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:31.120
You saved me, kid!

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:33.700
You're really okay?

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:36.750
What, you're worried about me?

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:39.120
I heard you didn't want to go into town,

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:40.620
so I thought you just didn't like people, but...

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:42.410
Hughes!

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:45.700
I can be worried when somebody's hurt.

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:47.410
I see, I see!

00:11:47.410 --> 00:11:50.040
Sorry!

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:51.250
You okay?

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:52.750
I'm fine, I'm fine.

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:55.410
Just missing some blood is all.

00:11:55.410 --> 00:11:57.330
Drink it. It'll make more blood.

00:11:57.330 --> 00:11:58.910
Thanks!

00:11:58.910 --> 00:12:01.000
I'll try some now...

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:02.620
It stinks!

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:05.950
It works. I guarantee it.

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:08.580
He's being nice. Drink it.

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:11.120
We can't have you collapsing.

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:13.950
We were very worried.

00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:15.500
Sorry!

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:24.290
Remember this, kid.

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:27.120
I'm Hughes, the duke's bodyguard.

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:31.700
If you need help, come to the town
of Gaunago and rely on me.

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:33.500
I'll be there for you.

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:35.040
Got it?

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:38.540
Got it!

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:41.450
They were nice people.

00:12:41.450 --> 00:12:44.450
My heart hurt a little.

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:48.000
Because I lied to them.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:51.620
I made up that story about my grandparents.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:55.200
Actually, the one who died three years ago...

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:56.870
...was me.

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:01.580
There'll be more slimes to come!

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:06.830
Now, how shall I get down?

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:10.410
You're such an idiot.

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:12.700
You're not done yet?

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:16.450
--I told you to get it done before I left!
--This is me, three years ago.

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:19.370
I'm a little older than I am now,

00:13:19.370 --> 00:13:21.250
--Takebayashi-san,
--and I live in a place
that's a little different.

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:23.200
--you're working overtime tonight, huh?
--and I live in a place
that's a little different.

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:24.250
--So am I!
--and I live in a place
that's a little different.

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:26.500
--Just get to work.
--One day,

00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:29.700
I found myself in a strange place.

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:34.540
So I'm dead. I see.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:35.950
Is that all?

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:41.870
Others who've come here
are typically more upset by this.

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:44.080
But you don't seem to be.

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:46.290
I am surprised.

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:50.120
But dreams end eventually.

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:53.620
And even if it's true, everyone dies one day.

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:59.910
I knew my current job
would kill me soon, anyway.

00:13:59.910 --> 00:14:03.160
I worked for what they call a black company.

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:04.410
Massive overtime.

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:06.200
--You idiot!
--Terrible bosses.

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:07.330
No days off.

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:09.870
I was exhausted.

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:12.000
Who are you, by the way?

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:14.370
Gods.

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:18.040
I am Gain the Creator.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:21.000
I am Lulutia, Goddess of Love.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:23.870
I am Kufo, God of Life.

00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:25.950
Nice to meet you all.

00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:28.200
I'm Takebayashi Ryoma.

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:31.910
Sorry, I don't have a business card...

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:33.500
We don't need one.

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:38.750
We're from a different world
than the Earth where you live.

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:41.160
What they call an "other world," yes?

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:43.950
Did you attain enlightenment or something?

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:47.580
I'm glad we don't have to
take the time to explain it.

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:50.910
You see it all the time in manga and anime.

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:51.950
But...

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:53.200
What?

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:55.750
How did I die?

00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:59.370
You hit your head and had a brain hemorrhage.

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:03.120
You sneezed when you were sleeping.

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:04.250
Four times.

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:07.410
With each sneeze, your pillow moved.

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:10.870
And finally, you hit your head on the floor.

00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:14.410
It burst several blood vessels in your brain.

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:16.620
And that was that.

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:18.950
That's not fair!

00:15:18.950 --> 00:15:22.040
How could I have died like that?!

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:25.000
The beer bottles from my drunk boss!

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:29.200
Even my dad's abuse! I survived all of that!

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:32.000
So how could I die from a sneeze?

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:33.830
Is that what freaks him out?

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:35.910
His cause of death was a shock, huh?

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:41.540
You had a secret pride in your toughness, huh?

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:44.370
I'm sorry.

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:45.910
I lost control for a moment.

00:15:45.910 --> 00:15:48.040
Please continue.

00:15:48.870 --> 00:15:53.290
I'll explain why I brought you here.

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:55.290
Because it's cliché.

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:57.120
I see! I'm going to another world!

00:15:57.120 --> 00:15:59.700
Do I go like this, or do I get
reincarnated 'cause I'm dead?

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:01.250
Do I have some job I'm supposed to do?

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:03.830
This really is going fast.

00:16:03.830 --> 00:16:07.370
You won't be starting from scratch, I suppose.

00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:10.660
You'll be entering a body I created.

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:16.450
You'll be around eight years old, though,
so maybe you could call it reincarnation.

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:17.410
Eight?

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:19.250
Your great task...

00:16:19.250 --> 00:16:21.250
No, you really won't have one.

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:22.330
So...

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:25.080
When we send you to our world,

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:27.540
we can make a hole in the wall
separating your world and ours.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:30.450
"The World of Earth" "The World of Seilfall"

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:30.450
we can make a hole in the wall
separating your world and ours.

00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:32.540
"The World of Earth" "The World of Seilfall"

00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:32.540
And when that happens, we'll send
the magical power from Earth to our world.

00:16:32.540 --> 00:16:35.870
"The World of Earth" "The World of Seilfall"
"Magical Power" "Ryoma's Soul"

00:16:32.540 --> 00:16:35.870
And when that happens, we'll send
the magical power from Earth to our world.

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:37.120
"The World of Earth" "The World of Seilfall"
"Magical Power" "Ryoma's Soul"

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:37.120
Magical power?

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:40.790
Our world is running out, you see.

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:43.080
So you need more.

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:44.080
Yes.

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:47.580
The Earth has magic, but nobody uses it.

00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:50.700
I see.

00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:52.540
Um...

00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:55.790
Can I use it when I get there?

00:16:55.790 --> 00:16:57.370
You sure can!

00:16:57.370 --> 00:16:59.450
Really?

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:02.580
Excuse me.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:04.660
If you're looking forward to it that much,

00:17:04.660 --> 00:17:08.500
shall we make it so you can
use all types of magic?

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:11.870
Wouldn't I stand out, then?

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:15.120
It's rare, yes.

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:17.910
But not that big a deal.

00:17:17.910 --> 00:17:19.330
But...

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:22.410
You tend to never be able to
really master any type.

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:24.370
I see.

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:28.450
After that, they gave me
a lot of advice and explanations.

00:17:28.450 --> 00:17:30.620
This is when I decided on the idea

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:33.750
that my grandparents had died
and I left the village.

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:35.000
I couldn't tell anybody that
I came from Earth, after all.

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:38.830
"Contract"
"Takebayashi Ryoma"

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:38.830
I couldn't tell anybody that
I came from Earth, after all.

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:48.700
Your new life is about to begin!

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:51.660
You don't need to be so
polite and formal all the time,

00:17:51.660 --> 00:17:54.200
and you can live the way you want.

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:56.080
The way I want...

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:57.250
I understand.

00:17:57.250 --> 00:17:59.410
I mean, got it!

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:02.330
We'll always be watching over you!

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:05.540
When you make it to town, go to the church.

00:18:05.540 --> 00:18:09.700
With the oracle skill, you can talk to us.

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:11.120
Roger.

00:18:11.120 --> 00:18:13.700
I won't forget to do that when I go to town.

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:16.330
Looks like it's time.

00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:19.620
Have a fun and exciting time!

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:25.910
Thank you... Thank you so much!

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:28.410
Here we go!

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:32.660
We open for you the gate to a new world!

00:18:32.660 --> 00:18:35.080
May you have our blessings!

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:37.830
May the light shine on your next journey!

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:43.120
And so I...

00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:54.750
I was reborn into this world, Seilfall,

00:18:54.750 --> 00:19:00.370
as Ryoma Takebayashi, age eight!

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:06.500
A child's body...

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:14.250
So this is the other world?

00:19:15.620 --> 00:19:21.790
The gods prepared
a manual for me for my new life.

00:19:21.790 --> 00:19:23.500
On the last page is my current status...

00:19:23.500 --> 00:19:26.040
"Your starting status is on
the last page of this book."
On the last page is my current status...

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:28.950
It's like an online game!

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:33.580
Though all my stats are for brute strength...

00:19:33.580 --> 00:19:35.870
But, well,

00:19:35.870 --> 00:19:39.580
I guess it means they kept
my skills from my last life.

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:56.750
I'm strong, but my body's a different size,
so I need to get used to it.

00:19:57.950 --> 00:19:59.700
A slime!

00:20:02.160 --> 00:20:04.040
Can it do tricks?

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:05.330
Show me your paw!

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:08.330
No luck, huh?

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:10.950
Oh, right! Magic!

00:20:10.950 --> 00:20:14.250
Um... "How to use magic.

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:16.370
To make a monster obey you,

00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:16.830
"Contract Procedures for Familiars"
"Notes"

00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:16.830
To make a monster obey you,

00:20:16.830 --> 00:20:18.660
"Contract Procedures for Familiars"
"Notes"

00:20:16.830 --> 00:20:18.660
you need taming magic to make a monster obey"...

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:20.950
"Contract Procedures for Familiars"
"Notes"

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:20.950
This is it! Um...

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:30.250
Calm your heart and feel the magic within you...

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:31.870
Feel it...

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:36.160
So this is magic?

00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:43.000
Once you feel it, envision it
flowing out of your body...

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:10.540
I decided to live within the Forest of Gana.

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:17.370
In my last life, it was impossible for me
to spend time on my hobbies.

00:21:17.370 --> 00:21:20.910
So maybe that's why I decided to
spend all my time researching slimes.

00:21:20.910 --> 00:21:25.370
And the first people I met
in this world after three years

00:21:25.370 --> 00:21:27.620
were Reinhart and his friends.

00:21:28.790 --> 00:21:33.080
Two weeks passed since they went back to town.

00:21:34.080 --> 00:21:35.540
Um...

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:39.080
Three hundred sixty-four sticky slimes.

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:40.330
And...

00:21:40.330 --> 00:21:42.950
There's way more of them than before.

00:21:42.950 --> 00:21:47.200
I was back to my usual life.

00:21:48.830 --> 00:21:50.950
This feels so good...

00:21:56.700 --> 00:21:57.580
What's wrong?

00:21:57.580 --> 00:22:01.200
Hey, Ryoma!

00:22:01.200 --> 00:22:03.160
How've you been?

00:22:07.700 --> 00:22:09.750
Ever since I came to Seilfall,

00:22:09.750 --> 00:22:12.540
my world was just me and my slimes.

00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:16.120
But now it was about to get a lot bigger!
